    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "redefining success feels like a joke. it just feels like settling. i dont want to \"explore new avenues\" or \"take a break,\" i want to be what i was. but i can feel myself becoming a parody of myself. it's actually exhausting to keep pretending i have anything left to give. it's better to just walk away now while i'm still respected than to keep dragging this out until i'm just some old guy making mediocre garbage.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
